---
// For Health Systems: the data-layer story in depth. Copy is from the brief (Hero C with guardrail edits,
// section 1 positioning lines) or owner-approved. See CLAUDE.md before editing.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SourcedStat from '../components/SourcedStat.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import CaptureSteps from '../components/CaptureSteps.astro';
import { EARLY_ACCESS } from '../site';

---

<BaseLayout
  title="For Health Systems — EdTerm"
  description="EdTerm captures how your most experienced clinicians reason, so that knowledge can inform the systems you use."
>
  <!-- Hero C (brief, with guardrail edits) -->
  <Hero
    label="For health systems"
    headline="The competitive advantage in healthcare AI won't come from the algorithm. It will come from what you train it on."
  >
    <p>
      One model doesn't fit every health system. Every organization has thousands of hours of clinical judgment built
      into how it runs, and that knowledge isn't in the EHR or the imaging data. It lives in people. To get the most
      from AI in your organization, it has to learn from the people who run it. EdTerm captures how your most
      experienced clinicians reason, so that knowledge can inform the systems you use.
    </p>
    <Button slot="actions" href={EARLY_ACCESS.href} size="lg">Start a conversation</Button>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Retention of experienced clinicians' knowledge -->
  <Section tone="white" heading="Keep what experienced clinicians know" id="retention">
    <p>
      EHRs and imaging record what happened. Genomic databases record what is possible. Neither records how an
      experienced clinician interpreted it.
    </p>
    <p>EdTerm captures that reasoning.</p>
    <!-- Connected sequence: a thin line joins the steps, left → right on desktop, top → bottom on mobile. -->
    <CaptureSteps slot="wide" tone="white" class="lg:mt-6" />
  </Section>

  <!-- What the database becomes (owner-approved copy, verbatim) -->
  <Section tone="white" heading="What the database becomes as it grows" id="database">
    <p>The Human Wisdom Database is a structured, searchable archive of how experienced clinicians reason.</p>
    <p>
      A product delivers an answer. Infrastructure is what answers are built on. The database doesn’t tell a clinician
      what to do. It holds the reasoning that decision support, clinical AI and training systems can reference.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each Wisdom Node adds to the archive. As it grows, it can show where experienced clinicians agree, where they
      differ, and why: patterns no single clinician could describe alone.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <!-- Decision support and training: longer-term uses -->
  <Section tone="paper" heading="Decision support and training, over time" id="longer-term">
    <p>Clinical AI, decision support and training systems can reference expert reasoning, not only outcomes.</p>
    <p>These are longer-term uses. The first step is capture.</p>
  </Section>

  <!-- Sourced statistic with count-up -->
  <section class="on-dark bg-deep py-section" aria-labelledby="turnover-heading">
    <div class="container-site grid-12 items-end gap-y-10">
      <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-7" data-reveal>
        <h2 id="turnover-heading" class="sr-only">The cost of RN turnover</h2>
        <SourcedStat
          value={5.19}
          decimals={2}
          prefix="$"
          suffix="M"
          label="Average annual hospital RN turnover cost"
          source="NSI National Health Care Retention & RN Staffing Report, 2026 edition (2025 data)"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="col-span-12 max-w-(--container-prose) text-lead text-white/85 lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9" data-reveal>
        <p>When experienced clinicians leave, their reasoning leaves with them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- One closing call to action -->
  <CTA heading="Early Access" buttonLabel="Start a conversation" />
</BaseLayout>
